===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|h₂epó}}{{root|en|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-}}
{{lbor|en|LL.|abligurrītiō|t=act of devouring; act of spending in feasting}}, from {{m|la|abligurriō|t=to lick away; (''figuratively'') to spend or waste indulgently, squander}} + {{m|la|-tiō|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|abstract noun}}s from {{glossary|verb}}s}}; from {{m|la|ab-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘away; away from; from’}} + {{m|la|ligurriō}}, {{m|la|liguriō|t=to lick up; to feast or feed upon; to be dainty or fond of luxuries}} (from {{m|la|lingō|t=to lick (up)}} + probably {{m|la|-uriō|pos=suffix meaning ‘to desire or wish’}}).<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|entry=† abligurition|pos=n|id=396|date=June 2021}}</ref>

