#* {{quote-book|en|author=J. E. L. Seneker|chapter=Letter V|editor=Thomas Stone|title=Frontier Experience: Or Epistolary Sesquipedalian Lexiphanicism from the Occident|edition=102nd anniversary|year=1906|year_published=2008|page=68|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=Icnbjs7a-MoC&pg=PT84|isbn=978-0-557-00391-4|passage=So soon as a rogation for a benison by the concionator, transpired, fourchettes, and all implements for the transportation of prog from the table to oral apertures, were movent and sonorific. Such '''abligurition'''; such lycanthropic edacity, lurcation, ingurgitation and gulosity; such omnivorousness and pantophagy; and such a mutation and avolation of comestibles, had never fallen under my vision in any antecedent part of my sublunary entity. Truly, anamnestic of [[w:Lord Byron|[Lord] Byron]]’s “dura illia messorum!”|footer={{small|A deliberate use of bombastic language.}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Bonnie Johnson|title=Wordworks: Exploring Language Play|location=Golden, Colo.|publisher=Fulcrum Resources|year=1999|page=103|isbn=978-1-55591-402-8|passage=Deipnosophy, not '''abligurition''', makes the aristologist.|footer={{small|A deliberate use of bombastic language.}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:John Green|title=w:An Abundance of Katherines|location=London|publisher=w:Penguin Books|year=2006|year_published=2012|page=46|pageurl=https://www.google.com/books?id=fyWxzvzaWgIC&pg=PT50|isbn=978-0-14-134610-6|passage=“Your dad says it’s because I remember things better than other people on account of how I pay very close attention and care very much.” / “Why?” / “Because it is important to know things. For an example, I just recently learned that Roman Emperor {{w|Vitellius}} once ate one thousand oysters in one day, which is a very impressive act of '''''abligurition''''',” he said, using a word he felt sure Katherine wouldn’t know.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Barbara Ann Kipfer|entry=abligurition|title=Word Nerd: More Than 17,000 Fascinating Facts about Words|location=Naperville, Ill.|publisher=[[w:Sourcebooks (publisher)|Sourcebooks]]|year=2007|page=3|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=h9zXAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA3|column=1|isbn=978-1-4022-0851-5|passage=[W]hen you squander your money on treats and comfort foods, you are engaging in '''abligurition''' (excessive spending on food and drink)}}

